id: pm-i7indd
title: "SDK: inject host-bound runtime into ImportExportContext"
description: "ImportExportContext lacks the host-bound ExtensionCommandSdk already available to CommandHandlerContext, forcing importer/exporter packages such as pm-todos to spawn the pm binary for core actions. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched all statuses for ImportExportContext, host-bound SDK, importer/exporter execution, and pm-todos spawning; pm-7qjk and pm-1p2u cover registration/test invocation, pm-xzhz covers the runtime, and pm-13bn covers migration, but none inject the runtime into importer/exporter handlers."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:extensions","area:packages","area:sdk",github-report
created_at: "2026-07-26T16:19:51.157Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:45:02.621Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T19:43:28.024Z"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#de74a49829faaec73e28ece0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: ImportExportContext exposes the same host-bound SDK contract needed for in-process core actions; importer/exporter test helpers can inject and exercise it; parity tests prevent CommandHandlerContext and ImportExportContext runtime capability drift; pm-todos can migrate away from spawning pm without private imports; SDK and extension docs describe the lifecycle and compatibility contract
goal: project management = context management
objective: Every extension execution surface receives composable in-process PM primitives from the public SDK
value: Package authors can build portable import/export integrations without subprocess coupling
why_now: GitHub issue #749 reports a real downstream pm-todos blocker after the SDK-first baseline landed
parent: pm-usfg
severity: medium
resolution: Host-owned ExtensionCommandSdk and portable workspace coordinates now flow through ImportExportContext.
expected_result: Importer/exporter handlers receive a typed host-bound SDK and can execute supported PM actions in process.
actual_result: Importer and exporter handlers receive the invocation-bound SDK and workspace coordinates; typed loader tests prove identity and compatibility.
component: sdk
